      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1931: New tradeoff introduced by the PS5 backpressure design (distinct from the earlier \u0027flood drops legitimate calls\u0027 note): at capacity you now return `Untracked` and *continue processing* instead of dropping. That is better for availability, but it disables dedup entirely for the overflow request: `deferMessageDedup` stays true so the top-level `isMessageTreated(req.id)` check is skipped, and the id is never inserted into `transientIOSCallRequests_`, so `reserveIOSCallRequest()` can never return `Duplicate` for its retransmissions. Under a flood, every duplicate DHT re-announcement of an untracked call request therefore re-runs `findCertificate` and re-invokes `iOSConnectedCb_`, which can report the same incoming call to CallKit multiple times — the exact double-signal this reservation set exists to prevent. Consider falling back to the shared `treatedMessages_`/`isMessageTreated` path for the untracked overflow case (i.e. only *defer* dedup when a reservation was actually taken), so overflow requests still get some duplicate suppression. If overflow is considered adversarial-only and thus acceptable, a short comment stating that would help future readers.",
      "revId": "be74ec1205476b773a03968af678b8c72a6652ae",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
